    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37581" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-ferrātus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>tipped</i> or <i>shod with iron</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">modius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pilum,</span>”
				<i>pointed with iron</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 10, 23, § 97</span></i>
			. —<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeferratus apud molas tribunus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>chained</i>, <i>fettered</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Pers. 1, 1, 22</span></i>
			.</div>
